          }
        }
      }
    },
    "user-agent.custom" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the User agent dropdown of the site panel and Settings › Privacy › Sites: the site is sent a user agent you typed.",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Custom"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "自定"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "user-agent.custom-action" : {
      "comment" : "Item at the end of the User agent dropdown in the site panel: opens a sheet to type the user agent this site is sent.",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Custom…"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "自定…"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "user-agent.edit-custom-action" : {
      "comment" : "Item at the end of the User agent dropdown in the site panel, once the site has a typed user agent: opens the sheet to change it.",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Edit Custom…"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "编辑自定…"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where ⌘T and links put a new tab in the sidebar." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under “New tabs open” in Settings › Tabs.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "⌘T 和链接打开的新标签页在边栏中的位置。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A page from a site with no tabs open goes at the top." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under “New tabs open” in Settings › Tabs when Next to Tabs from the Same Site is chosen.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "没有打开标签页的网站，新页面放在顶部。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A page from a site with no tabs open goes at the bottom." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under “New tabs open” in Settings › Tabs when Next to Tabs from the Same Site is chosen.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "没有打开标签页的网站，新页面放在底部。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A page from a site with no tabs open goes next to the current tab." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under “New tabs open” in Settings › Tabs when Next to Tabs from the Same Site is chosen.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "没有打开标签页的网站，新页面放在当前标签页旁边。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "#%lld on GitHub" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of an issue number at the end of a point in What’s New, like “#32 on GitHub”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "GitHub 上的 #%lld"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ %@" : {
      "comment" : "Joins two sentences, one after the other. Leave out the space if your language doesn't put one between sentences.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@%2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ %@ at %@.png" : {
      "comment" : "A captured picture's file name: the page's title, the day (2026-11-21) and the time (14.03.22).",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@ at %3$@.png"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@ %3$@.png"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ %lld-bit" : {
      "comment" : "A certificate's public key on the certificate page of the site panel: its type, then its size in bits, like “RSA 2048-bit”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$lld-bit"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$lld 位"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "A button's tooltip: its name, then its keyboard shortcut in parentheses, like “Reload (⌘R)”.\nWhere a download rule sends links: the service's address, then its method in parentheses, like “127.0.0.1 (load.start)”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ (%2$@)"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@（%2$@）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ (System)" : {
      "comment" : "The first choice of Translate pages into, in Settings › Translation: the Mac's language, by name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@（系统）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ afternoon" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a History session that began in the last week. The placeholder is the weekday, like “Tuesday”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@下午"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ afternoon, %@" : {
      "comment" : "Name of an older History session: the weekday, then the date, like “Sunday afternoon, October 18”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ afternoon, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%2$@ %1$@下午"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ and %@" : {
      "comment" : "Under a space's name in Settings › Spaces: its pinned tabs, then its open tabs, like “3 pinned tabs and 2 open tabs”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ and %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ 和 %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ and all its subdomains." : {
      "comment" : "Preview of a domain rule.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 及其所有子域名。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ and pages below it, such as %@/repo." : {
      "comment" : "Preview of a path rule.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ and pages below it, such as %2$@/repo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ 及其下的网页，例如 %2$@/repo。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ are handed to %@" : {
      "comment" : "A download rule in a sentence: what it catches, then the script it is given to. The placeholders are the two parts.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@交给 %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ are saved to %@" : {
      "comment" : "A download rule in a sentence: what it catches, then the folder its files are saved into. The placeholders are the two parts.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@会保存到 %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ at %lld%%" : {
      "comment" : "Beside Page Size among the developer tools above the page, while a page larger than the window is shown smaller to fit: its size, then how large it's shown, like “1440 × 900 at 72%”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@，缩放至 %2$lld%%"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ beta %@" : {
      "comment" : "A beta of Zigzag as people read it: 0.9.2 beta 1. The placeholders are the version and the beta's number.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ beta %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ Beta %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ can be your search engine" : {
      "comment" : "Toast after adding an extension that gives a search engine. The name is the engine's, like ChatGPT.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "可以把 %@ 设为你的搜索引擎"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ can’t be deleted yet" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the sheet shown instead of the one that deletes a profile, while an import or an extension is still going into that profile. The placeholder is the profile's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "暂时无法删除“%@”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ can’t hear this tab. Its sound is protected or can’t be reached." : {
      "comment" : "Toast when an extension asks to hear a tab whose sound Zigzag can't hand it (protected video, or sound it can't reach). The placeholder is the extension's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 无法收听这个标签页：它的声音受保护或无法获取。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ can’t listen to this tab while %@ is. Turn %@ off for this tab, then try again." : {
      "comment" : "Toast when an extension asks to hear a tab another extension is already listening to; only one can at a time, as in Chrome. The first placeholder is the extension that asked, the other two the one listening, like Sound Booster.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ can’t listen to this tab while %2$@ is. Turn %3$@ off for this tab, then try again."
