      "comment" : "Choice in the Page Appearance menu of the developer tools above the page: the page is asked for its dark look.\nColor choice in Reader.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "深色"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dark Pages" : {
      "comment" : "Toolbar button tooltip in the PDF viewer. Shows the pages dark.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "深色页面"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dark already" : {
      "comment" : "Short, it fits beside a dropdown. Under Dark page in the site panel's This Site group: dark pages are on, and the site has a dark look of its own, so it's left as it is.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "本身就是深色"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dark page" : {
      "comment" : "Row in the site panel's This Site group: draws this site's pages dark.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "深色网页"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dark pages" : {
      "comment" : "A setting in Settings › Appearance: websites without a dark look of their own are drawn dark.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "深色网页"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Darkest" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver, the Shade slider's value at its deepest.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "最暗"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Data" : {
      "comment" : "Under a site in Settings › Privacy › Site Data: what it keeps on this Mac. A label, no full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "数据"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Data from a profile that’s no longer listed" : {
      "comment" : "Title of a row in Settings › Profiles, for data left on this Mac by a profile that's in no list.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "来自已不在列表中的个人资料的数据"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Default" : {
      "comment" : "The name of the first profile, which holds what Zigzag kept before there were profiles, until it's renamed.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "默认"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Default Browser" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in an Open URL download rule's Open in dropdown: opens the web address in the Mac's default browser, as these rules did before Zigzag had its own places.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "默认浏览器"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Default browser" : {
      "comment" : "A setting in Settings › General.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "默认浏览器"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every window on a space lists the same tabs, each showing its own. A page can be on screen in one window at a time." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under “Windows share a space’s tabs” in Settings › Tabs.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "同一空间的每个窗口列出相同的标签页，各自显示自己的那一个。一个网页同一时间只能显示在一个窗口中。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "What This Allows…" : {
      "comment" : "Button on the apps-on-this-Mac setting in Settings › Privacy: reopens the briefing.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "此功能允许什么…"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Websites you switch on in Site Controls can use fetch, XMLHttpRequest and WebSocket to reach programs listening on this Mac, over loopback only.\n\nThe local network, other machines, images, scripts and stylesheets are not included, and a page cannot switch itself on.\n\nA local program may not have been written to be reachable by a web page, and a site you grant could use it in ways you did not intend. Only grant sites you trust.\n\nTurn one site off in its Site Controls, or turn this setting off for every site." : {
      "comment" : "The briefing shown before websites may reach apps on this Mac. fetch, XMLHttpRequest and WebSocket are API names: keep them as they are.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "你在网站设置里开启的网站可以使用 fetch、XMLHttpRequest 和 WebSocket，与这台 Mac 上监听端口的程序通信，且只限本机回环。\n\n不包括本地网络、其他机器，也不包括图片、脚本和样式表，页面也无法自行开启。\n\n本机程序未必是按网页可以访问来设计的，你授予的网站可能会以你意料之外的方式使用它。只授予你信任的网站。\n\n在某个网站的网站设置里关掉它，或关掉这个设置，对所有网站生效。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
